# Copy to secret_internal_api.env in this same folder and fill in a real
# value - generate one with:
#   python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
#
# Shared with chat_app's own secret_internal_api.env (same value on both
# sides) - this token authenticates internal calls between chat_app and
# mcp_server (e.g. POST /upload) where there's no human login, so it is the
# entire authorization for that one route - treat it like a password.
INTERNAL_API_TOKEN=
